The '''douyin_scraper''' is a Python-based tool designed to scrape and filter metadata from a list of Douyin videos, while also downloading the videos. It takes a list of video URLs and a set of metadata filters as input, and outputs a CSV file containing the filtered metadata along with the downloaded videos. The tool utilizes the '''douyin-tiktok-scraper''' library to interact with the Douyin API.

== Overview ==
The '''douyin_scraper''' is a command-line tool that provides a simple and efficient way to collect and analyze Douyin video metadata. It is designed to be easy to use, with a minimal number of dependencies and a straightforward installation process.

=== Features ===
The '''douyin_scraper''' has several key features, including:
* The ability to download Douyin videos from a list of URLs
* The ability to extract and filter metadata from the downloaded videos
* The ability to output the filtered metadata in a CSV file
* The use of the '''douyin-tiktok-scraper''' library to interact with the Douyin API

== Installation ==
To install the '''douyin_scraper''', follow these steps:
# Clone the repository using '''git clone https://github.com/Clemapfel/douyin_scraper.git'''
# Install the required dependencies using '''pip install json''', '''pip install csv''', '''pip install requests''', and '''pip install douyin-tiktok-scraper'''

== Usage ==
To use the '''douyin_scraper''', follow these steps:
# Collect the video URLs and paste them into a file, such as '''video_ids.txt'''
# Specify the metadata filters and paste them into a file, such as '''filter.txt'''
# Execute the script using '''python3 scrape.py video_ids.txt filter.txt'''
# Collect the output, which will include a CSV file containing the filtered metadata and a folder containing the downloaded videos

=== Example Usage ===
For example, to collect the metadata for a list of Douyin videos, you can create a '''video_ids.txt''' file containing the following:
```
https://www.douyin.com/video/7188679476946029885
https://www.douyin.com/video/7188514977211305277
https://www.douyin.com/video/7188463948864261434
```
You can then create a '''filter.txt''' file containing the following:
```
digg_count
play_count
share_count
```
Finally, you can execute the script using '''python3 scrape.py video_ids.txt filter.txt''' to collect the metadata and download the videos.

== Dependencies ==
The '''douyin_scraper''' depends on the following libraries:
* '''json''': for parsing JSON data
* '''csv''': for outputting CSV files
* '''requests''': for making HTTP requests to the Douyin API
* '''douyin-tiktok-scraper''': for interacting with the Douyin API

== Output ==
The '''douyin_scraper''' outputs a CSV file containing the filtered metadata, as well as a folder containing the downloaded videos. The CSV file will have a name in the format '''YYYY-MM-DD_hh:mm.csv''', and will contain the values for all keys specified in the '''filter.txt''' file. The folder will contain the downloaded videos, as well as a set of '''raw.json''' files containing the raw metadata for each video.